      "body": "Fixes #44278\n\n### Motivation\n\n`calculate_metrics` in `python/sglang/benchmark/serving.py` computed `Peak concurrent requests` as the max over per-second buckets: every integer-second bucket touched by a request (from start second through end second) was incremented, then the max was taken. That accounting over-counts requests that never run at the same time:\n\n- five sequential requests inside one second reported a peak of 5 instead of 1;\n- a request ending exactly when another starts reported a peak of 2 instead of 1 (double-counted boundary handoff).\n\nSo the reported \"Peak concurrent requests\" could exceed the benchmark's configured `--max-concurrency`, as seen in the run recorded in #14165 (`Max request concurrency: 1` but `Peak concurrent requests: 2`).\n\n### Modifications\n\n- In `calculate_metrics`, keep the per-second `concurrent_requests_per_second` bucket array for the `--plot-throughput` plot, but compute the scalar `max_concurrent_requests` with a sweep line over half-open `[start, end)` intervals of successful requests: end events sort before start events at the same timestamp, so touching intervals do not count as overlapping.\n- Unchanged: per-second plot statistics, output-token throughput, average concurrency, and the \"Peak concurrent requests\" printout label — only the scalar peak is now truthful.\n\nThe Rust client's `peak_windows` (`rust/sglang-bench/src/metrics.rs`) shares the same bucket accounting; left out of scope here so the change stays CPU-verifiable, noted as a follow-up.\n\n### Tests\n\n- Issue's CPU-only repro (from the issue body) against the real `calculate_metrics`, with heavy deps (`torch`, `transformers`, `aiohttp`, ...) stubbed via `sys.modules`: sequential-within-one-second now reports 1 (was 5), boundary handoff reports 1 (was 2), genuinely-overlapping control still reports 5 — all pass.\n- Additional edge cases verified: staggered/nested overlaps (peak 3), chained touching intervals (peak 1), failed requests excluded, overlaps spanning multiple seconds — all pass.\n- `ruff check --select F401,F821,F823,UP037`, `ruff format --check`, `python3 -m py_compile`, and `git diff --check` all pass on the touched file.\n- No GPU on this machine; end-to-end benchmark runs and the Rust client change were not exercised here — a maintainer CI run (`--ask-ci`) would be appreciated.\n\n<!-- pr-states:start -->\n---\n### CI States\n\nLatest PR Test (Base): <!-- slot:pr-test:start -->:x: [Run #38747827607](https://github.com/sgl-project/sglang/actions/runs/38747827607)<!-- slot:pr-test:end -->\nLatest PR Test (Extra): <!-- slot:pr-test-extra:start -->:x: [Run #38747827286](https://github.com/sgl-project/sglang/actions/runs/38747827286)<!-- slot:pr-test-extra:end -->\nLatest PR Test (AMD ROCm 10): <!-- slot:pr-test-amd:start -->:x: [Run #38747827346](https://github.com/sgl-project/sglang/actions/runs/38747827346)<!-- slot:pr-test-amd:end -->\n<!-- pr-states:end -->",
